    "summary": "Powerful second set with High Time and Pigpen‑rich jams",
    "blurb": "The second set shines on a clean soundboard capture of Good Lovin', China Cat > I Know You Rider, High Time and Turn On Your Lovelight. Pigpen’s organ is front‑and‑center, especially during the Me & My Uncle tease and his own numbers. The first half suffers from modest audio hiccups in one source but the playing stays solid.",
    "review": "On November 21, 1969 at Cal Expo’s Building A, the Dead delivered a second set that still feels fresh for any Deadhead. Both soundboard tapes agree that the band was locked into a tight groove – “fat, cross‑road guitar tone” from Jerry bridges the Live Dead and Working‑Man’s Dead eras, while Pigpen’s Fender organ weaves a snaky, almost Dylanesque texture through the Me & My Uncle tease and his own showcases. Highlights cascade from a rousing Good Lovin' into a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, then surge forward with a crisp High Time and a soulful Turn On Your Lovelight that lets Pigpen’s keyboards truly shine.\n\nThe first half of the show is marred on one recording by muddy early tracks, but the musical performance never wanes. The second set’s energy, strong transitions, and prominent Pigpen moments make this night a must‑listen for fans of the late‑’60s era, especially those who love hearing the organ front‑and‑center amid classic Dead repertoire.",
